        <h3>Getting audio onto OpenSwim is a chore.</h3>
        <p>Shokz OpenSwim and OpenSwim Pro store music on 4 GB of internal flash with no Bluetooth and no streaming. To load audio, you plug them into your Mac and manually drag files in Finder, exporting from Apple Music, renaming files that break on FAT32, and hoping nothing corrupts mid-transfer.</p>
        <div class="compare-visual compare-visual--today" aria-label="Drag and drop illustration">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" fill="none" style="width: 100%; max-width: 380px; height: auto;">
